/-!
# VII16 — the finite asymptotic bridge (sufficiency direction)

Real germs on `(0, ε)` whose iterated derivatives `0 … n` have finite right limits at the
origin. Glue the negative side to the Taylor polynomial of those limits. The result is a
genuine `Cⁿ` function on `(-ε, ε)` agreeing with the germ on the positive side — exactly the
regularity interface `FiniteBranch6` needs.

**The derivative limits are an INPUT.** `notes/VII16_ASYMPTOTIC_ANALYSIS.md` records that the
paper's §3.1 supplies value-level asymptotics (Eq. 30/33) and a *chosen* formal integer-power
series (Eq. 32/36), not derivative asymptotics. The converse (paper branch ⇒ these limits) is
not established in this round, so the original goal stays conditional.
-/

